    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe device web portal takes ~5 seconds to fully load due to 11 separate JS/CSS files loading sequentially over HTTP/1.1 from PROGMEM. During this time the user sees a blank or partially-rendered page with no feedback.\n\n## Proposal\n\nInline a lightweight \"Loading, please wait\u2026\" indicator directly in the HTML `<body>` of `index_html.hpp` (before any external JS/CSS loads). Once `app.js` initialises, it hides/replaces the splash with the real UI.\n\nThis is purely a perceived-performance improvement \u2014 the actual load time stays the same, but the user gets immediate visual feedback that the device is responding.\n\n## Context\n\n- Observed during #232 hardware verification (v0.0.12-beta.2)\n- Portal serves 11 gzipped PROGMEM assets sequentially (~190-210ms each)\n- Total waterfall: ~2-3s for assets + ~600ms for API calls\n- No errors \u2014 just a UX gap",
